# Keep byte-anchored file classes LF in the working tree on every platform.
# Windows checkouts (core.autocrlf=true) were converting these to CRLF,
# which silently breaks: byte-anchored patchers (python, reading with
# newline=""), the verify_engine.sh chain replay, and any .sh invoked from
# WSL ("set: pipefail\r: invalid option name"). Blobs are already LF;
# this only fixes checkout behavior. CI (Linux) is unaffected.
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.py  text eol=lf
*.c   text eol=lf
*.h   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
